WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.970
Spring Storm

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:20.110
He's coming from the right!

00:02:20.410 --> 00:02:21.120
This way?

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:22.530
No, the left!

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.240
Which way is it?

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.580
YOUR left, Ota!

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.040
Where's Izumi?
Where's unit 1?

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.380
Huh? Izumi? Uh...

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.550
Damn you!

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:49.310
Out of my way, Izumi!

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:50.940
Let me handle it.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.900
Use your baton to disable it.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:57.110
You can destroy his leg actuator!

00:02:58.150 --> 00:02:59.820
You talk too much.

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:04.780
Ota, how could you?

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:06.120
Move it! Finish him off!

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:10.330
Take that!
And that and that!

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.680
Poor Alphonse.

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.390
There was no reason to
go on a shooting spree.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.400
The two of you could
have held it easily.

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:37.270
Easy for you to say.
You weren't there!

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.150
That's always your excuse.

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:40.950
It's odd, how you ALWAYS
have to use your gun.

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.160
Don't mock me, Shinohara!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:45.030
It's my fault.

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:48.870
If I hadn't hesitated...

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:49.790
Yeah!

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.790
Listen, Shinshi.
I know you're inexperienced.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.750
But don't give out orders
that only make things worse!

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:59.000
That's enough, Ota.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.270
Don't pay any attention to him.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.190
Sure, except that he's right.

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.450
Factory Labor:   Bulldog

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:30.660
What's that, Shinshi?

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:35.920
Our reaction times, indexed to the
Labor models we were up against.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:39.920
It might be a useful reference
on future mobilizations.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.670
Too cool!

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:44.840
You should have gone
into computer work!

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.220
Oops, that didn't come out right.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.180
Special Vehicles, Second Section.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:55.020
Shinshi, phone.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:56.900
Hello, Shinshi here.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:04.860
Not at all.
It's just so out of the blue.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.450
I don't believe my eyes.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.580
Just finishing today's report.

00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:11.700
Very impressive.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.040
Won't you have to
reorganize now?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:15.790
Why?

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.210
Everyone's already serving
in their ideal post.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:22.300
Kanuka Clancy left
a pretty big hole.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:25.880
Yes. It's a good opportunity.

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.930
Are you tired or something?

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.440
No, just a little zoned out.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:38.480
I'll go splash some water
on my face and snap out of it.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.200
Ota, sorry about
what happened out there.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.120
I know I caused you
a lot of trouble.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.540
Just get up to speed.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:02.960
And I'll try hard not to
follow your orders till then.

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:03.550
Right.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:05.630
The good stuff's already gone!

00:06:05.630 --> 00:06:06.720
I'm sorry!

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:09.130
It isn't your fault.

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.720
Stop apologizing all the time.

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:16.430
You can't be like that
in this business.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:21.770
Maybe I should change jobs.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.950
Mr. Mikiyasu Shinshi, I suppose?

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:33.490
I'm Yoshikawa.
I spoke to you on the phone.

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:35.200
Pleased to meet you.

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.370
After graduation...

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:42.040
you were a programmer
for a brokerage for five years.

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:46.920
In the winter of '97,
you left to join the police force.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:51.760
That April, you aced the entrance
exam and had three weeks training.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:55.260
Worked in Special Vehicles,
Second Section until present.

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:58.060
Did I miss anything?

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:59.180
No, nothing.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.860
Don't take it the wrong way.
I'm just doing my job.

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:07.110
I'll come straight to the point.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.400
A certain venture is very
interested in hiring you.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:14.280
A software development start-up.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.250
It's only 2 years old, but
it's doing extremely well...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.830
and is turning heads in the industry.
Are you interested?

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:23.500
I dunno.
I'd have to think about it.

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.210
I understand.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:29.470
But are you satisfied
with your current job?

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.760
Better yet, are you needed?

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:34.010
Well...

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:36.100
You're the right man
in the right place.

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:39.680
I'm just someone
who wants to help.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:43.190
They'll triple your current salary.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:45.150
And you'd be a department head.

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:48.650
Triple? Department head?

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.200
We should start giving it
some serious thought.

00:07:54.570 --> 00:07:55.370
Yeah.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.660
Listen, Tamiko...

00:07:59.290 --> 00:07:59.910
Yes?

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.120
Um, we need to talk.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.840
It's my miso soup.
It's too salty, isn't it?

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:08.090
Oh, no.

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:10.010
- It's delicious.
- Oh, good!

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:11.130
So anyway...

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:11.590
Yes?

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.720
Our house is getting
too small for us.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:17.100
Don't you ever wanna move?

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:18.810
Oh, no!

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:21.640
As long as we're together,
I'm happy!

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.190
A condo's fine.
I don't need a big house.

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:27.230
Our mortgage is hard enough now.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:32.400
Sure, I'm sick of having such
nosy neighbors, but it's okay.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.610
It's something
you have to live with.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:35.910
I'm sure I'll get by.

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.660
It's hard on you though.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.500
All the wives in the neighborhood
know your salary...

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.670
and the department rumors.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.920
Sorry I've put you through this.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.340
You're so nice to me!

00:08:49.340 --> 00:08:51.550
Don't worry. I'll get by, really.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.510
So long as we're together,
we can put up with anything.

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:56.930
I guess.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.430
Noa, brace your right leg!

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:10.770
Grab her left arm!
Then...

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:11.780
Then what?

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:14.070
Block him!
Move your left leg!

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:15.700
Done and done!

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.820
Watch out for her leg!

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.280
What?

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:32.630
Good plan, huh, having
a practice match for the new duo?

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.170
Too bad the wrong side won.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:50.560
What's wrong?

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:53.070
Do you have a moment?

00:09:58.860 --> 00:09:59.950
Let's go outside.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.910
Relax, would you?

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.420
I don't think I can do this.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:17.130
I can't lead Ota, and I think it's hard
for him to take orders from me.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:19.010
You're both doing fine.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:23.890
Sure, complaints are up,
but at least the arrests aren't down.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:26.060
Nothing to worry about.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.190
The arrests are all to Ota's credit.

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:31.100
They weren't my doing.

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:34.520
The forward and
backup share the credit.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:36.940
You've only started
working together.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:39.360
Give it some time
before you make a judgement.

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.700
Stick with it a bit longer.

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:52.210
I'd like a little more time
to think it over.

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:53.960
No, it's not that.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:55.840
Yeah.

00:10:56.670 --> 00:10:58.880
Besides, I haven't spoken
to my wife about it yet.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.590
Really? When?

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:02.890
All right.

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.640
Right, until then.

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:12.060
How come you're hiding
on the phone?

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.610
Uh, actually...

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.610
Aha!
That was your wife!

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.740
You're such a devoted husband.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:28.410
I'm home.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:35.170
Who is this Yoshikawa woman?

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:36.670
Why?

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.260
Who is she?

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.510
Oh, hello.
It's gotten warmer out, hasn't it?

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:44.390
Sure has.

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:48.600
What's the meaning of this?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:49.810
Wait...

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:53.650
I've tried to make our home
a place of honesty and trust.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:57.860
We promised not to have any
secrets between us, remember?

00:11:57.860 --> 00:12:02.610
And now I find out you're
planning to change jobs!

00:12:02.700 --> 00:12:05.410
- You know?
- That woman told me!

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:08.290
She wants you to call.
I don't know exactly what about.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:12.500
I don't want you to do it.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:14.210
I love this home!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:17.090
The housewives in this
complex are so nice!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:19.050
I couldn't bear to
move away from them!

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.840
Tamiko, calm down!

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.760
I <i>am</i> calm!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:25.010
In fact,
I've never been calmer!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:27.010
Uh, what about my dinner?

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.610
Griffin

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:45.160
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:12:47.120 --> 00:12:48.240
Long time, no see.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:50.950
Izaki, what are you doing here?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.540
This isn't the typical protocol.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:58.130
But your future employer
wanted to meet you.

00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:00.500
In fact, he insisted.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:02.670
It's <i>Izaki's</i> company?

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:05.510
Correct.
I'll leave you gentlemen alone.

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:09.010
- Surprised?
- Yeah.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.770
I knew you'd left the brokerage
to start a company.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.890
But I never thought
we'd meet again like this.

00:13:16.980 --> 00:13:20.400
We need the cream of the crop.

00:13:21.730 --> 00:13:24.150
No B.S. How's your job?

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:27.700
Come on, Shinshi!
Why don't you join me!

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:31.740
She told me about the job,
but I haven't made up my mind yet.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:35.330
The department head
was just our initial offer.

00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:37.580
But I think you might be suited
for an executive position.

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:41.170
Izaki. I'm hardly
what you'd call a leader.

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:44.050
You greatly
underestimate your talents.

00:13:44.630 --> 00:13:46.760
I think you could do it.
What do you say?

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:51.640
- It's an offer you can't refuse.
- True.

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.930
Drink up.

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:54.100
Let's celebrate.

00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:02.940
Letter of Resignation

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.100
Have something to eat.

00:14:40.520 --> 00:14:42.900
It's not healthy to starve yourself.

00:14:43.570 --> 00:14:46.860
I need to make up my mind
about the job today.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.200
I'll be home later.

00:15:07.090 --> 00:15:08.300
Yummy.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.060
Shinshi,
is that all you're having?

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.440
You look pale.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.020
Not enough nutrition!

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:24.610
Here, have my hard-boiled egg.

00:15:25.400 --> 00:15:26.020
Eat up.

00:15:26.980 --> 00:15:28.570
Thank you.

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:32.740
Physical strength is the foundation
of intellect and energy!

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:35.120
You can't do your duty
if you're weak!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.040
Sure, but he doesn't have to
make it sound so harsh.

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:41.160
Well.
That's just the way Ota is.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:42.790
His heart's in the right place.

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.360
Captain’s Office

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:20.410
What's up?

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:24.370
You look so serious.

00:16:25.130 --> 00:16:27.420
I'd like to speak with you.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.590
Not bad news, I hope.

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:34.430
Oops, I guess
this'll have to wait till later.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:43.690
Attention pilot! We have you
completely surrounded!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.400
Give up and surrender peacefully!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:50.980
I repeat. We have you
completely surrounded!

00:16:51.480 --> 00:16:54.070
Give up and surrender peacefully!

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:03.910
Why won't they give us
the orders to move in?

00:17:04.290 --> 00:17:08.750
The SWAT team said they didn't
want to agitate the terrorist.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:12.010
He already looks
plenty agitated to me!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:14.050
So do you, come to mention it.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:15.260
Am not!

00:17:15.550 --> 00:17:18.600
They're sure keeping us roped in.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.510
How so?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:23.730
It's like the SWAT team wants
to have first crack at this.

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.440
Politics as usual, right.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:30.980
HQ is filled with
departmental rivalries.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:35.400
If we swoop in
and clean up this mess...

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:38.240
we'll make
the SWAT team look bad.

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.700
You sound like a suit, Shinshi.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.200
Out of our way!

00:17:42.200 --> 00:17:43.620
Real men, coming through!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.080
But maybe you were right.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.090
We'd better move back.

00:18:07.520 --> 00:18:09.020
Shall I send my men out?

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:11.730
Send in the APC!

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:28.080
He's getting away!

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:31.250
Shinshi,
any orders from the captain?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:32.170
Not yet.

00:18:32.920 --> 00:18:35.710
All units, retreat!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.220
He's heading for the grade school!

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:41.590
What?

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.890
What's the captain doing?

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:45.770
Can they evacuate the school
in time?

00:18:47.230 --> 00:18:49.600
Don't just stand there,
you waste-of-space!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:55.400
Ota, board your unit!

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:56.530
We're moving out!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:59.450
But we haven't got orders yet!

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:03.410
You have, from your backup!
You gonna disobey me?

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:06.660
No, sir!
I'm boarding my unit!

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:17.760
I'll obstruct its feet and
slow it down, so you can catch up.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:19.220
Roger.

00:19:24.680 --> 00:19:26.600
- The rest of you follow them.
- Roger.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:28.810
We're moving out, team!

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:29.850
Can we?

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:32.600
Someone has to stop those two.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:33.350
Right.

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.170
Shinshi!

00:19:57.550 --> 00:19:59.130
Ota, shoot him!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.590
What?

00:20:01.590 --> 00:20:02.880
You want to shoot, don't you?

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.220
I know you really want to
fry this creep!

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.100
Well, I order you to shoot!

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.600
Hang on, Shinshi!

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:11.520
Miss and you'll regret it!

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:19.440
He's moving too much!
I'll never hit him!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.280
Take good aim and shoot him!
Hurry!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:25.110
Shoot him!

00:20:27.410 --> 00:20:28.660
Shoot him!

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:45.300
Noa, go!

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.550
All right!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.310
You're dead!

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.860
And that's a wrap.

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:06.570
I'm very sorry, but I'll
have to decline your offer.

00:21:06.950 --> 00:21:07.870
Yes, right.

00:21:08.410 --> 00:21:10.990
I kind of figured you'd pass it up.

00:21:11.950 --> 00:21:18.380
You love being a cop
more than you might realize.

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:25.510
Nice work out there.

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.010
Captain!

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:29.510
You finally seized control.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:36.190
You have to fight fire with fire,
that's for sure.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.770
We can forget about that talk
we were going to have, I assume?

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.030
Yes.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:45.110
Hang in there a little longer.

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:47.320
A little longer?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:54.290
Tamiko?

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:56.040
Welcome home.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:58.210
What are you doing?

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.670
Getting ready to move.

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:01.920
Move? Why?

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:05.090
Cause you're getting a new job!

00:22:05.470 --> 00:22:08.220
We got this place through your
department, so we'll have to leave.

00:22:08.220 --> 00:22:09.430
Oh, the new job.

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:11.300
I turned them down.

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:15.980
I gave it a lot of thought,
and I'm not cut out for office work.

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:22.320
You mean, you decided
without me AGAIN?

00:22:23.190 --> 00:22:28.990
I already said goodbye
to all our neighbors!

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:31.910
I can't say we're staying now!

00:22:31.910 --> 00:22:34.580
You're always making
decisions without me!

00:22:34.580 --> 00:22:36.540
Tamiko, calm down!

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:38.000
Tamiko, please!

00:22:42.460 --> 00:22:45.670
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.800 --> 00:22:49.380
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.720 --> 00:22:55.640
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.060 --> 00:23:05.150
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:08.070
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.150 --> 00:23:12.660
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.330
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.410 --> 00:23:20.160
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:24.340
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.510 --> 00:23:30.840
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:36.100
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.060 --> 00:23:38.640
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.850
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.100 --> 00:23:45.940
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.320 --> 00:23:52.110
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.280 --> 00:23:58.160
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:04.790
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.460
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:09.460
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:14.680 --> 00:24:18.390
A new recruit comes to train
with our team: Takeo Kumagami.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:22.310
She came to Division Two
at her own request.

00:24:22.310 --> 00:24:25.190
She's great with computers,
cooking and so much more!

00:24:25.190 --> 00:24:28.190
- I can't keep up!
- You should watch your step.

00:24:28.190 --> 00:24:31.280
Captain says she's great with Labors.
She might become a forward!

00:24:31.280 --> 00:24:32.110
You serious?

00:24:32.110 --> 00:24:34.280
Coming next: I'm Takeo Kumagami.

00:24:34.530 --> 00:24:36.120
Target: Locked on!

00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:41.160
Next episode

00:24:36.160 --> 00:24:41.160
I’m Takeo Kumagami
